WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
HOME STUDIO | MY HOME, INSIDE HOME ASSISTANT
My real home and installed tools. Now let’s build a new room from a photo.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.000
START WITH A PHOTO AND REAL MEASUREMENTS
This fictional room is our reference. The tutorial uses a separate, empty Home Assistant project.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.000
01 | START INSIDE HOME ASSISTANT
Open Home Studio in the HA sidebar. Start with a blank project and choose Draft from photos.

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:28.000
02 | CONNECT YOUR OWN AI PROVIDER
The API key stays masked on screen. HA holds it for this session and sends it only to authenticate with the provider.

5
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
03 | GIVE THE PHOTO A SCALE
Enter known width, depth and ceiling height. Explain which wall, door and window you are looking at.

6
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
04 | ADD THE REFERENCE PHOTO
Review the selected photo. It is sent to your chosen model only when you press Generate.

7
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:49.000
05 | A REAL REQUEST, WITH VALIDATION
The first draft puts a sofa outside the room. Validation rejects it without changing the drawing.

8
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:58.000
06 | RETRY WITH THE SUGGESTED CORRECTION
A second real request returns a valid draft. Waiting time is shortened here.

9
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.000
07 | REVIEW, THEN APPLY
Inspect the proposed room in 3D. It becomes editable only after you choose Apply.

10
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:13.000
08 | REFINE THE ROOM SIZE
Change the room to 5.5 × 4.5 m. Save draft commits the edits while leaving the published view unchanged.

11
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:20.600
09 | MOVE FURNITURE ON THE GRID
Select the coffee table and drag it. Snap aligns it to the 0.25 m grid; exact coordinates stay visible.

12
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:25.600
10 | SET EXACT DIMENSIONS
Set the table to 1.10 × 0.65 × 0.45 m. The same object updates in the 3D preview.

13
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:32.600
11 | POSITION ITEMS DIRECTLY IN 3D
Choose Edit items and drag the table across the floor. Orbit remains a separate tool.

14
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:38.920
12 | FIND THE RIGHT VIEW
Orbit the room to see the selected item and its vertical handle clearly.

15
00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:43.920
13 | RAISE AN OBJECT
Drag the vertical Y handle to lift the table 0.50 m above the floor.

16
00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.920
14 | MAKE A FINE ADJUSTMENT
Hold Alt and press Arrow Up for a precise 1 cm height step. Alt also bypasses the grid while dragging.

17
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:54.920
15 | LOWER IT TO AN EXACT HEIGHT
Enter 0.25 m, then 0 m to return the table to the floor. You stay in control of the final placement.

18
00:01:54.920 --> 00:02:01.920
16 | CONNECT A HOME ASSISTANT DEVICE
Select the floor lamp and link the demo light entity. This tutorial controls no physical devices.

19
00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:08.920
17 | SAVE, THEN PUBLISH
Save the editable draft. Publish it when you are ready to update the household’s 3D Home.

20
00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:17.680
18 | USE THE ROOM YOU CREATED
Open 3D Home and switch the linked demo light on. The room responds to its real HA entity state.

21
00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:25.680
19 | RETURN TO EDITING ANYTIME
Choose Edit home to continue the saved drawing. Built and recorded inside Home Assistant, using v0.10.1-beta.6.
